        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "URBANIZATION ECONOMIES (Jacobs externalities):\n  Benefits from the SIZE and DIVERSITY of\n  the city -- regardless of your industry.\n  Named after Jane Jacobs.\n  Jacobs (1969): \"The Economy of Cities\"\n  -- diversity of industries cross-fertilizes\n  ideas; new sectors emerge from combination\n  of existing ones (brassiere industry in NYC:\n  emerged from women entering\n  garment industry + need for support).\n  Example: NYC's diverse economy."
    },
    {
